@startuml flash-write
' Erasing and programming the spare bank. Grounded in Src/flash.c and
' RM0351 Rev 9, sections 3.3.5 to 3.3.8.

title One update session, seen from the flash driver

skinparam shadowing false

start
:BEGIN arrives, the image fits;
:spare bank = the one NOT running\n(from SYSCFG FB_MODE);
note right
  MER1 and MER2 erase PHYSICAL banks.
  FB_MODE decides which physical bank
  is seen at 0x08000000, so the bit is
  chosen from the running bank, never
  from an address (RM0351 3.5).
end note
:wait BSY, unlock with KEY1 then KEY2,\nclear the error flags;
:set MER1 or MER2, set START, wait BSY;
if (any error flag set?) then (yes)
  :lock, flush the data cache;
  :NAK FLASH_ERROR, session ends;
  stop
else (no)
  :lock, flush the data cache;
  :ACK;
endif

repeat
  :DATA at the expected offset;
  if (offset and length are multiples of 8,\nand inside the bank?) then (no)
    :refused without touching flash;
    :NAK FLASH_ERROR;
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
  :unlock, then for each double word:\nclear errors, set PG, write low word,\nwrite high word, wait BSY;
  :lock, flush the data cache;
  :ACK;
repeat while (more DATA?) is (yes)
->no;

:COMMIT;
:CRC-32/ISO-HDLC over the image\nREAD BACK from the spare bank;
note right
  Read back, not accumulated as the
  bytes arrived: that is what catches
  a byte that never reached flash.
  The data cache was flushed, so this
  reads flash and not stale cache.
end note
if (matches the CRC32 from BEGIN?) then (no)
  :NAK VERIFY_FAILED, session ends;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:switch banks (piece 7);
note right: until piece 7 this refuses,\nso a good run ends in NAK FLASH_ERROR
stop

@enduml
